.TH "HTMLMEDIAELEMENT.ENCRYPTED_EVENT" "3JS" "July 28, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
HTMLMediaElement.encrypted_event \- HTMLMediaElement: encrypted event
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[CR]encrypted\f[R] event is fired when initialization data is
found in the media that indicates it is encrypted.
.PP
This event is not cancelable and does not bubble.
.SH SYNTAX
Use the event name in methods like \f[CR]addEventListener()\f[R], or set
an event handler property.
.IP
.EX
addEventListener(\(dqencrypted\(dq, (event) => { })

onencrypted = (event) => { }
.EE
.SH EVENT TYPE
A \f[CR]MediaEncryptedEvent\f[R].
Inherits from \f[CR]Event\f[R].
